SlicerDSpace reconstructs anatomy directly from diffusion MRI, without a T1-weighted scan.

3
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:17,150
It maps microstructure, from DTI to free water, NODDI and kurtosis.

4
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,000
Tissue labels.

5
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:22,600
Brain regions.

6
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:26,150
White and pial surfaces,

7
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:28,522
all in native diffusion space.

8
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:33,818
Whole-brain tractography, traced in the same native space.

9
00:00:38,800 --> 00:00:42,024
White-matter bundles, from the same tractogram.

10
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:47,331
And structural connectomes, built on the same anatomy.

11
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:54,100
One 3D Slicer module, with automatic QC and a record of every run.

12
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:04,449
SlicerDSpace. Brain anatomy from diffusion MRI, inside 3D Slicer.
